      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We analyze the given inequality $\\sin(x+y)\\leq \\sin(x)+\\sin(y)$ by considering the range of sine and the sum of angles in trigonometry. To do this, let's start by defining an expression that can be used to check the inequality for any $x$ and $y$ in the interval $[0,\\pi]$. \n\nThe sum of angles in a sine function can be an upper bound, using the linear property of sine function $\\sin{(A+B)}\\leq \\sin A+\\sin B$, see [1] (always false, due to special cases). Applying this, we get that \n$$f(x, y) = \\sin(x) - \\sin(x+y) + \\sin(y)$$\nis always negative for $x$ and $y$ in the given interval, because both $\\sin(x)$ and $\\sin(y)$ are strictly greater than $-1$, as well as $|y|<\\frac{x}{2}\\leq \\frac{\\pi}{2}$. Consequently, $f(x, y)<0$ for any $x, y\\in [0,\\pi]$. This leads to\n$$\\boxed{y\\in [0,\\pi], x\\in [0,\\pi]}$$\n\nIn a game, 0.88 of the players scored 3 points each and the rest scored 1 point each. If a player scored 3 points, they get to choose the next question's theme. Given that 300 players took part, and they had 10 questions, if each choice takes an average of 60 seconds, how much time did players spend choosing themes if they decided the themes 30 times in total?\n\nTo determine the total time spent by players choosing themes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the number of players who scored 3 points.\n2. Calculate the number of questions each type of player would have to answer.\n3. Determine how many turns of choosing themes each player needed for all questions.\n4. Calculate the total time spent by all players on choosing themes.\n\nFirst, we know that 0.88 of the players scored 3 points each and the rest scored 1 point each. There are 300 players in total.\n\nThe number of players who scored 3 points is:\n\\[ 0.88 \\times 300 = 264 \\]\n\nThe number of players who scored 1 point each is:\n\\[ 300 - 264 = 36 \\]\n\nEach turn of choosing themes covers 3 questions with 3 players scoring 3 points each and 36 players scoring 1 point each. The total number of turns needed is:\n\\[ \\frac{10 \\text{ questions}}{60 \\text{ seconds per turn}} = \\frac{10}{60} = \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ turns per question} \\]\n\nSo, the total number of turns needed for all questions is:\n\\[ 10 \\text{ questions} \\times \\frac{1}{6} \\text{ turns per question} = \\frac{10}{6} \\text{ turns} \\]\n\nSince each turn requires one choice and a choice takes 60 seconds, the total time spent by all players is:\n\\[ \\frac{10}{6} \\text{ turns} \\times 60 \\text{ seconds per turn} = 100 \\text{ seconds} \\]\n\nThus, the total time players spent choosing themes is:\n\\[ \\boxed{100} \\]",
